  "meta-title": "Bathroom Sign in Sheet Builder, Free to Start | Emergent",
  "meta-description": "Build a bathroom sign in sheet students tap on a classroom tablet, or a cleaning log staff open from a code on the restroom door.",
  "name": "Build a Bathroom Sign in Sheet for Passes and Cleaning Checks",
  "description": "Build a bathroom sign in sheet that logs student passes or restroom cleaning checks, with the time saved on each entry.",
  "awb---mockup-data": "<p id=\"\">window.awbMockup = { classroomPasses: \"I teach 7th grade science, and my class shares one restroom pass. Build a bathroom sign in sheet on a tablet by the door where each student taps their name to leave and taps again when they are back. While one student is out, show the next student that the pass is in use and who has it, and save the time out and the time back.\", cleaningChecks: \"We clean the customer restroom at our fuel stop every 2 hours while the store is open. Build a cleaning check that staff open by scanning a code on the restroom door. List 6 tasks to tick: toilets, sinks, soap, paper towels, floor, and trash. Ask for initials and save each check with the time it was finished.\", problemReports: \"Our library has a code on each restroom door. Build a form where a patron picks the problem from a short list, such as a clogged toilet or no paper towels. Post each report to our facilities channel in Slack with the restroom and the time, and let the custodian mark it fixed.\", multiSiteReview: \"We run 6 cafes, and each one has 8 restroom checks a day, 56 a week. Build a weekly view for the district manager that shows the checks each cafe logged out of 56. Flag any cafe that logged under 50, so the manager knows which store to call on Monday.\" };</p>",
  "awb---how-to-title": "How to Create a Bathroom Sign in Sheet",
  "awb---how-to-description": "Seven steps to create a bathroom sign in sheet that records each pass or cleaning check with its time, then build it with Emergent.",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Bathroom Sign-In Sheet FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a bathroom sign in sheet?\", \"a\": \"A bathroom sign in sheet is a log of who used or serviced a restroom, and when. Classrooms keep one for student passes, with a name, a time out, and a time back. Businesses keep one as a cleaning record, with the check time, the tasks done, and the initials of whoever did them.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a bathroom sign in sheet?\", \"a\": \"Decide whether it logs passes or cleaning checks, then list the fields: a name and two times for passes, or tasks and initials for cleaning. Describe that, plus any rule such as one student out at a time, to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the sheet, the database behind it, and the views you asked for.\"}, {\"q\": \"What columns does a bathroom sign in sheet need?\", \"a\": \"A pass sheet needs the student's name, the time out, and the time back, plus a destination if students also visit the nurse. A cleaning sheet needs the date, the check time, one column per task, and the initials of the person who did the work.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a bathroom sign in sheet be separate from other classroom sign-ups?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A restroom pass changes every few minutes and needs a time on each entry, while a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/club-sign-up-sheet'>club sign up sheet</a> collects names once and stays the same for weeks. Keeping them apart leaves the pass log short enough to read at a glance during a lesson.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should staff fill in a bathroom sign in sheet for cleaning?\", \"a\": \"Match it to traffic. A busy fuel stop or cafe might check every 2 hours while open, and a small office might check twice a day. Put the check times on the sheet in advance. A missed check then shows as an empty slot instead of a line nobody remembered to add.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a bathroom sign in sheet limit how many students are out at once?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when the sheet tracks the pass instead of only listing names. You set the number allowed out of one room, and it can differ by class period, such as two during a long lab. When the limit is reached, the next student sees who is out and waits.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a free bathroom sign in sheet template enough for a classroom?\", \"a\": \"For one pass and no rules, a blank template on a clipboard works. It falls short once you want to see who has the pass right now, or count trips by week. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing a live version. The same builder makes other shared lists, such as a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/potluck-sign-up-sheet'>potluck sign up sheet</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I get staff to use a bathroom sign in sheet on every check?\", \"a\": \"Make logging faster than skipping it. Put the code where the work ends, on the door on the way out, and list only tasks the attendant does anyway. Go over the weekly log with the team, gaps included, and ask about each missed check while the shift is still fresh in mind.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a bathroom sign in sheet show patterns over a semester?\", \"a\": \"Yes, once entries are rows instead of handwriting. The sheet Emergent builds saves each pass to a database you own, class period included. Count trips by student or by week. Treat a pattern as a reason to talk with the student, never as a verdict on its own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who should initial a bathroom sign in sheet after cleaning?\", \"a\": \"Whoever did the cleaning, with their own initials, at the moment they finish. One shared login, or one person signing for a whole shift, hides who checked what. Fire drills and safety trainings belong on a separate <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/safety-sign-in-sheet'>safety sign in sheet</a>, which records attendance rather than tasks.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
  "afb---prompt": "<p>Build a bathroom sign in sheet for my 7th grade classroom where each student taps their name to leave and taps again when they are back.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build a bathroom sign in sheet for my 7th grade classroom where each student taps their name to leave and taps again when they are back.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Classroom Passes\", \"add\": \"Add one pass per room, so a second student waits until the first taps back in.\"}, {\"label\": \"Cleaning Checks\", \"add\": \"Add a cleaning check opened from a code on the door, with six tasks and initials.\"}, {\"label\": \"Problem Reports\", \"add\": \"Add a problem report from the restroom door that posts to the facilities channel in Slack.\"}, {\"label\": \"Multi-Site Review\", \"add\": \"Add a weekly view of cleaning checks by location that flags any site under 50.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
